[[File:E 499.png|thumb|[[Baron Seal]], the first example of a Colossus enemy]]
'''Colossus Enemies''' (超生命体 ''Chō Seimeitai'', '''Super-Lifeforms'''), also known as '''Colossal Enemies''' or '''Colossi''', are a type of [[Enemy Units|Enemy Unit]] introduced in [[Gauntlet]]s, [[Uncanny Legends]], and the [[Zombie Outbreaks]] of Cats of the Cosmos Chapters 2 and 3. All Colossus enemies also have one of the standard enemy types alongside Colossus. In terms of design, Colossus enemies are modified versions of their existing counterparts and, likewise, tend to be more powerful than the original, with large black orbs embedded somewhere within them.

Certain Colossus enemies are used as bosses and the main threat of their respective Gauntlets. They often boast monstrous stats, an assortment of abilities to help them push and powerful support units appearing alongside. In the case of Gauntlet-exclusive bosses, they and their support gain progressive stat boosts in each subsequent fight.

Like [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]], [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] and [[:Category:Kaijin Enemies|Kaijin]], Colossus is not considered a trait, meaning it always overlaps with one of the standard enemy types. The only ability to specifically affect Colossus enemies is [[:Category:Colossus Slayer Cats|Colossus Slayer]], which increases damage against them to 1.6x and reduces damage taken from them to 0.7x. Colossus Slayer stacks with any anti-trait stat-based abilities (Strong/Massive Damage/Insane Damage/Resistant/Insanely Tough), allowing for massive stat boosts under the right circumstances.

Units with Colossus Slayer [[Talent Orbs]] gain an anti-Colossus stat buff on every second deployment depending on the Orb's Rank. However, it does not stack with the Colossus Slayer ability, as the maximum bonus given by the Orbs is identical to what said ability already provides. When two Colossus Slayer Orbs are equipped by the same unit, only the highest-ranked one takes priority.

