==Trivia==
*[[Baron Seal]], [[Le'Grim]], [[Mega-Mooth]], [[Super Hyppoh]], [[Archangel Exiel]] and [[Big Peng Z]] were introduced before the Colossus type itself and thus did not have it until [[Version 11.2 Update|Version 11.2]], which added the Colossus type and retroactively applied it to these six enemies.
*The descriptions of the Colossus [[Gauntlet]] bosses follow a pattern: First, they state that a secret lab used genome editing to enhance non-Colossus versions of the enemies. Then, they mention the main [[Special Abilities]] of the enemies. Finally, they state that the enemies gain increasing lethality after each battle.
**The only exceptions to this is [[Gigahaniwan]], whose English description omits the increasing lethality part at the end, likely as a result of the in-game character limit being more restrictive for the English version due to the differences between the Japanese and English languages.
*Colossus enemies were not listed in the [[Enemy Guide]] until [[Version 11.3 Update|Version 11.3]], making them the first enemies whose descriptions were added retroactively.
*Most of the major Colossus enemies' Japanese descriptions incorporate the names of their respective stages:
**[[Baron Seal]]'s states that he requires maximum '''caution''' (警戒), the Japanese name of the [[Baron Seal Strikes/Red Alert 1~20|Red Alert]] levels.
**[[Le'Grim]]'s states that he has gone on a '''rampage''' (暴走), as in the [[Le'Grim Strikes/Rampage Lv1~20|Rampage Lvs]].
**[[Mega-Mooth]]'s states that he '''flies''' (飛来し) while blowing his enemies away, referencing [[Mega Menace/On Mighty Wings Lv1~20|On Mighty Wings]]' Japanese name, '''Flight''' (飛来).
**[[Super Hyppoh]]'s calls her an '''invader''' (侵略者), referencing [[Horrorpotamus/Cosmic Juggernaut Lv.1~20|Cosmic Juggernaut]]'s Japanese name, '''Invasion''' (侵略).
**[[Archangel Exiel]]'s states that he '''blesses''' (祝福) those who have lost their way, as in the [[Divine Archangel Strikes/Blessing Lv.1~20|Blessing Lvs.]]
**[[Big Peng Z]]'s states that he '''wanders''' (徘徊) the lands, as in the [[Big Peng Z Strikes/Wandering Lv.1~20|Wandering Lvs.]]
**[[Zero Luza]]'s states that it came to be when [[Great Ape Luza]] took in energy said to be the '''origin''' (起源) of all things and '''awakened''' (覚醒) its true power, referencing [[Revival of Origin]]'s Japanese name, '''Awakening of Origin''' (起源の覚醒).
**[[Omens]], [[Gigahaniwan]] and [[Jumbo Jones]] are the exceptions. Omens' description does not directly corelate to the stage names, as it quite literally translates to '''Three Figures'''(三体), merely referring to how they and their original variant consist of three entities, rather than just one. While Gigahaniwan's states that it was '''excavated''' (発掘) from ruins, the term used is different from the Japanese name of the [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!/Excavation Lv.1~20|Excavation Lvs.]] (出土): 発掘 merely implies it was discovered via excavation, while 出土 refers to being unearthed and taken from the ground.
*[[Super Hyppoh]]'s Japanese description implies that she is the same character as [[Hyppoh]], which would make her the only known female Colossus.
*[[J.J. Jackrabbit]] is the first Colossus enemy to:
**Appear outside of Gauntlets.
**Lack its own Gauntlet.
**Be a peon rather than a singular threat.
**Have had the Colossus type from the start rather than gaining it retroactively.
*As mentioned before, many Colossus enemies are created through genetic experimentation in the [[Laboratory of Relics]].
**[[Zero Luza]] appears to be the only exception, being the only Colossus enemy whose "core" is green rather than black. Its Japanese description does not mention genome modification nor the Laboratory of Relics, which suggests it to be a naturally-occurring one.
*Every Colossus enemy's Japanese name contains a word pertaining to size or magnitude.
*All Colossus enemies are variants of already-existing enemies, and they all possess the same trait(s) as their original counterparts. 
**[[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] and [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] are the only standard types not to have a Colossus Gauntlet boss, and Metal is the only standard type to not have a Colossus at all. 
*Prior to the [[Version 13.3 Update]], all Colossus enemies except [[Omens]], [[J.J. Jackrabbit]], [[Great Angel Chibinel]] and [[Zero Luza]] were listed as "Colossal" rather than "Colossus" in the [[Enemy Guide]].

